$docs = [
    'finance-guide' => [
        'title' => 'Finance Module User Guide',
        'sections' => [
            ['heading' => 'Overview', 'content' => 'The Finance Module is the central hub for all financial operations within the bus transport management system. It provides comprehensive tools for monitoring revenue, generating detailed reports, managing driver remittances, and performing financial audits. This module is designed specifically for finance staff and administrators who need to track the financial performance of bus operations in real-time. The system captures every financial transaction from fare collections to expense tracking, ensuring complete transparency and accountability across all operations. Users can access real-time data dashboards, generate period-specific reports, and maintain a complete audit trail of all financial activities. The module integrates seamlessly with other system components including passenger management, trip scheduling, and driver management to provide a holistic view of the organization\'s financial health.'],
            ['heading' => 'Accessing the Finance Dashboard', 'content' => "Step 1: Log in to the system using your finance staff or administrator credentials.\nStep 2: From the main navigation menu on the left sidebar, click <a href=\"/finance/dashboard.php\">Dashboard</a>.\nStep 3: The dashboard will load and display key performance indicators including total revenue, completed trips, pending remittances, and recent alerts.\nStep 4: Use the filter options at the top of the dashboard to narrow down data by date range, specific bus, driver, or route. Select your desired filter values from the dropdown menus.\nStep 5: Click the \"Apply Filters\" button to update the dashboard with your selected criteria. The charts and stats will refresh automatically.\nStep 6: To view the revenue trend chart, locate the chart section on the dashboard. Use the toggle buttons above the chart to switch between daily, weekly, or monthly views.\nStep 7: Hover over any data point on the chart to see the exact value for that period.\nStep 8: Quick-action buttons are located on the right side of the dashboard."],
            ['heading' => 'Generating Revenue Reports', 'content' => "Step 1: From the finance dashboard, click <a href=\"/finance/revenueOverview.php\">Profit Overview</a> from the sidebar menu.\nStep 2: The Profit Overview page displays with multiple report sections. The main chart shows revenue trends over time.\nStep 3: To customize the report period, locate the date range picker at the top of the page. Select your start and end dates, then click \"Apply\" to update the data.\nStep 4: To view route profitability, scroll to the \"Route Profit\" section. This table shows each route with its total revenue, number of trips, and average revenue per trip.\nStep 5: To compare bus performance, find the \"Bus Performance\" section. It displays revenue data for each bus in the fleet, sorted from highest to lowest.\nStep 6: For location-based insights, check the \"Location Insights\" section which breaks down revenue by boarding points and destinations.\nStep 7: To export the report, click the \"Export\" button at the top right of the page. A dropdown will appear with format options.\nStep 8: Select \"Export as CSV\" if you want to analyze the data in a spreadsheet application like Excel.\nStep 9: Select \"Export as PDF\" if you need a formatted document for printing or formal reporting.\nStep 10: The file will be downloaded automatically. Save it to your desired location on your computer.\nStep 11: To generate a scheduled report, click the \"Schedule Report\" button. Set the frequency (daily, weekly, monthly), recipients, and format, then click \"Save Schedule\"."],
            ['heading' => 'Managing Driver Remittances', 'content' => "Step 1: Navigate to <a href=\"/finance/remittance.php\">Remittance</a> from the sidebar menu.\nStep 2: The Remittance page displays a list of all driver remittances. The default view shows pending remittances that have not been settled yet.\nStep 3: Use the filter options at the top to search by driver name, bus number, date range, or status (Pending, Paid, Discrepancy).\nStep 4: Each row in the remittance table shows the driver name, trip details, expected amount (calculated by the system), and the actual amount to be remitted.\nStep 5: To mark a remittance as received, click the \"Mark as Paid\" button next to the remittance record.\nStep 6: A confirmation dialog will appear. Review the details and click \"Confirm\" to record the payment.\nStep 7: If the actual amount differs from the expected amount, click the \"Report Discrepancy\" button instead. Enter the actual amount received and a reason for the difference.\nStep 8: To view remittance history for a specific driver, click the driver\'s name to open their remittance history page showing all past remittances.\nStep 9: To generate a remittance report, click the \"Export Report\" button at the top. Select your desired format (CSV or PDF) and date range.\nStep 10: The report will be downloaded with complete remittance details for the selected period."],
            ['heading' => 'Verifying Online Payments', 'content' => "Step 1: Navigate to <a href=\"/finance/online_payment_verification.php\">Online Payment Verification</a> from the sidebar menu.\nStep 2: The page shows two tabs: \"Pending\" for new payments waiting for review, and \"Resubmissions\" for payments that were previously rejected and re-uploaded by the passenger.\nStep 3: By default, the Pending tab is active. Here you can see all GCash and hybrid payments that need verification.\nStep 4: Each pending payment row shows the passenger name, bus number, fare amount, GCash amount, payment method (GCash or Hybrid), and a \"View\" button to see the payment screenshot.\nStep 5: To review a payment, click the \"View\" button in the Proof column. A modal will open showing the passenger\'s GCash payment screenshot.\nStep 6: Examine the screenshot carefully to verify the payment details match the trip information.\nStep 7: If the payment is valid, click the green \"Approve\" button. A confirmation dialog will appear - click \"Yes, Approve\" to confirm.\nStep 8: If the payment is invalid or the screenshot is unclear, click the red \"Reject\" button. Confirm the rejection in the dialog.\nStep 9: The page will refresh, and the verified payment will move to the History tab.\nStep 10: Switch to the \"Resubmissions\" tab (if available) to review payments that passengers re-uploaded after rejection. The process is the same as approving or rejecting pending payments.\nStep 11: Switch to the \"History\" tab to review all previously verified payments. History shows both approved and rejected payments with the verifier\'s name and verification date."],
            ['heading' => 'Using the Audit Trail', 'content' => "Step 1: Navigate to <a href=\"/finance/history.php\">Remittance History</a> from the sidebar menu.\nStep 2: The Remittance History page displays a chronological log of all financial transactions and system activities.\nStep 3: Each entry in the audit log shows the date and time of the action, the user who performed the action, the type of action (e.g., Payment Verified, Remittance Paid, Report Exported), and a detailed description of what was changed.\nStep 4: To search for specific entries, use the search bar at the top of the page. You can search by username, action type, or keywords.\nStep 5: To filter by date range, use the date picker to select your start and end dates, then click \"Filter\".\nStep 6: To filter by user, select a username from the user filter dropdown to see only actions performed by that person.\nStep 7: To export the audit log, click the \"Export\" button and select your preferred format (CSV or PDF).\nStep 8: Review the exported audit log for compliance reporting or external audit requirements."],
            ['heading' => 'Exporting Financial Reports', 'content' => "Step 1: Navigate to <a href=\"/finance/exportandaudits.php\">Exports and Audits</a> from the sidebar menu.\nStep 2: The page provides options for generating comprehensive audit packages and exporting financial data.\nStep 3: To generate a complete audit package, click \"Generate Audit Package\". A configuration form will appear.\nStep 4: Select the date range for the audit package using the date picker fields.\nStep 5: Check the boxes for the sections you want to include: Revenue Summary, Trip Logs, Remittance Records, Discrepancy Reports, and System Activity Logs.\nStep 6: Select the export format - PDF for formal documentation or CSV/Excel for data analysis.\nStep 7: Click \"Generate\" to create the audit package. The system will compile all selected data into a single document.\nStep 8: Once generated, the file will be available for download. Click the \"Download\" button to save it to your computer.\nStep 9: All exported documents are automatically logged. To view your export history, click \"Export History\" at the top of the page.\nStep 10: In the Export History page, you can see all previously generated exports with their document ID, date, and format. Click on any entry to re-download the file."],
        ],
